  <name>Tunneler</name>
  <summary>Dig tunnels, hunt the enemy tank</summary>
  <developer id="com.kaniansky">
    <name>Norko Kaniansky</name>
  </developer>
  <description>
    <p>
      TUNNELER 2.0 (1991, Geoffrey Silverton) rewritten from its decompiled source: two tanks dig through
      an underground world, each seeing only a small window around itself, hunting each other with
      cannon fire while energy and shields run down. It plays exactly like the original DOS game - the
      same movement, digging, explosions, sound and look.
    </p>
    <p>On top of that:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Split screen for two players on one keyboard or two gamepads, like the original</li>
      <li>Skirmish: you against 1 to 7 computer tanks (easy, medium, hard), free-for-all or in teams</li>
      <li>Online games with up to 8 tanks: a list of games, lobbies with seats, teams and chat, spectators</li>
      <li>Game modes: gold rush, infection, survival, king of the hill, shrinking world, capture the flag, base siege, deathmatch</li>
      <li>Line of sight: see only around your tank, or only what dirt and rock don't hide</li>
      <li>Small, medium and large maps, rounds to win, a round time limit, friendly fire</li>
      <li>English, Slovak, Czech, Ukrainian and Russian</li>
    </ul>
  </description>
